text:
JWT `exp` = seconds. `Date.now()` = milliseconds. Comparison always wrong.

**Bug:**
```js
if (Date.now() > payload.exp) // Date.now() ~1700000000000, exp ~1700000000 → never expires
```

**Fix:**
```js
if (Date.now() / 1000 > payload.exp) // or: Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000)
```

**Full middleware:**
```js
function authMiddleware(req, res, next) {
  const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(' ')[1];
  if (!token) return res.status(401).json({ error: 'No token' });

  try {
    const payload = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET); // verify() checks exp auto
    req.user = payload;
    next();
  } catch (err) {
    return res.status(401).json({ error: err.message });
  }
}
```

Better fix: ditch manual check. `jwt.verify()` handle expiry auto — throws `TokenExpiredError` if stale. Manual `exp` check only needed if decode without verify (don't do that).

If must manual check:
```js
const now = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);
if (now > payload.exp) return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Token expired' });
```
